messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI assistants become routine in knowledge work and public services.",
      "detail": "Productivity rises unevenly, and regulation debates intensify over safety, privacy, and labor impacts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Fully reusable heavy-lift orbital rockets cut launch costs by an order of magnitude.",
      "detail": "This enables large on-orbit assembly, megaconstellations, and ambitious planetary missions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Clean energy becomes the majority of new power capacity worldwide.",
      "detail": "Wind, solar, storage, and grid upgrades dominate additions; new internal combustion vehicle sales fall sharply in major markets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Gene-editing and mRNA therapies are mainstream for several common diseases.",
      "detail": "Personalized treatments reduce burdens of cancers and inherited disorders; ethical and access frameworks mature."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "General-purpose AI reaches human-level performance on most professional benchmarks.",
      "detail": "It becomes a ubiquitous collaborator, reshaping education, law, software, and science; job roles reconfigure rather than vanish overnight."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "First grid-connected fusion demonstrator exports net power for sustained periods.",
      "detail": "Costs remain high, but confidence grows that fusion will complement renewables later in the century."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "A novel respiratory pathogen triggers a rapid global response and is contained within a year.",
      "detail": "Networked biosurveillance and fast vaccine platforms prove decisive, strengthening global health treaties."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "International AI safety and audit standards are adopted by major powers.",
      "detail": "Third-party evaluation, incident reporting, and compute accountability become routine, reducing systemic risk."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "A limited, time-bound stratospheric aerosol injection trial is conducted under UN oversight.",
      "detail": "It slightly lowers peak temperatures and informs risk models; governance and equity debates intensify."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Precision fermentation and cultivated meat overtake conventional livestock in many markets.",
      "detail": "Global land use shifts toward rewilding and biomass carbon removal; rural economies realign."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Sea level rise of roughly 0.25-0.5 meters stresses coasts worldwide.",
      "detail": "Coastal defenses, managed retreat, and insurance reforms accelerate; heat and water extremes drive migration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A permanent, internationally operated lunar base begins industrial pilot projects.",
      "detail": "Ice-derived propellant production and radio-quiet astronomy anchor a cislunar economy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Longevity therapies add a decade or more of healthy life expectancy on average.",
      "detail": "Chronic disease incidence declines; pension and labor policies adapt to longer working lives."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Space-based solar power demonstrators deliver steady gigawatt-scale power to grids.",
      "detail": "Microwave beam control and orbital construction mature, and commercialization begins cautiously."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Advanced AI planning and robotics automate large swaths of production and services.",
      "detail": "Many countries implement guaranteed income or negative income tax and lifelong learning; inequality remains a political focal point."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Global population peaks near 10-11 billion and begins a gradual decline.",
      "detail": "Urban densification, education, and healthcare drive low fertility; ecosystems begin partial recovery."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Mars hosts continuous settlements numbering in the low thousands.",
      "detail": "Closed-loop life support, in-situ resource use, and high-latency AI enable scientific and industrial outposts, not yet self-sufficient."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming stabilizes near 2-2.7 C; adaptation is widespread but uneven.",
      "detail": "Some coral, ice, and forests are irreversibly altered, while carbon removal and rewilding expand."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Deliberate solar radiation interventions are wound down as carbon removal scales.",
      "detail": "Long-horizon restoration of coasts, soils, and biodiversity takes priority."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Asteroid mining and cislunar industry supply niche materials and in-space construction.",
      "detail": "Orbital habitats house tens of thousands; Earth remains the demographic and cultural center."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Cumulative sea level rise reaches roughly 0.6-1.1 meters.",
      "detail": "Many low-lying regions are abandoned or elevated; new coastal cities are built with amphibious design."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Global governance features enforceable climate, biosafety, and AI compacts with broad participation.",
      "detail": "Conflicts persist but are shorter and less destructive due to automation, transparency, and economic interdependence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "High-fidelity brain-computer interfaces and digital personhood gain legal standing.",
      "detail": "Hybrid human-digital teams become common in research and governance; new debates on rights and identity arise."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Autonomous in-space factories replicate and expand infrastructure with strict safeguards.",
      "detail": "Through verified limits and auditing, runaway replication risks are kept low while reducing costs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Reliable fusion-fission-breeder and solar power back a largely post-scarcity energy economy.",
      "detail": "Desalination, materials recycling, and vertical agriculture close many resource loops."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Multiple self-governing habitats and planetary settlements achieve durable self-sufficiency.",
      "detail": "Cultural divergence accelerates, yet common law and translation protocols preserve interoperability."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Beamed-sail interstellar probes return high-resolution data from several nearby systems.",
      "detail": "No crewed interstellar travel yet, but navigation, shielding, and autonomy technologies mature."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Human cultures, languages, and lineages have diversified substantially across Earth and space.",
      "detail": "Religions and philosophies adapt to synthetic minds and off-world life; archives preserve deep history."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Large-scale ecosystem engineering creates closed biospheres on select moons and habitats.",
      "detail": "True planetary terraforming remains beyond practical timescales, but local environments thrive."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Population across the solar system reaches into the hundreds of millions to low billions.",
      "detail": "Trade flows primarily in knowledge and designs; heavy industry stays mostly off Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Human-descended populations show significant genetic and cybernetic divergence.",
      "detail": "Medical compatibility layers enable reproduction and mind interfaces across lineages."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Civilizational institutions survive multiple cycles of expansion and contraction without global collapse.",
      "detail": "Redundant archives, education compacts, and risk management reduce tail risks from war, plagues, and misaligned systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "A handful of interstellar outposts or slow-generation habitats exist, tenuously self-sustaining.",
      "detail": "They remain culturally linked by entangled institutions and centuries-long communication relays."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Orbital power and habitat networks capture a noticeable fraction of solar output without enclosing the Sun.",
      "detail": "Earth's climate is actively managed to offset gradual solar brightening and residual carbon feedbacks."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Outcome range: a resilient multipolar solar civilization persists, or earlier catastrophes have reduced humanity to a smaller, regionally bounded remnant.",
      "detail": "In either case, unmistakable human signatures remain in geology and orbital infrastructure; complete extinction by this date is possible but not the median forecast."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity likely stabilizes climate impacts, integrates powerful AI under governance, and expands across the solar system over millennia, with Earth remaining the cultural core. Civilizational capacity waxes and wanes, but redundancy and risk management improve long-run survival odds; limited interstellar presence is plausible by the far future. Extinction remains possible, yet a diversified, multipolar civilization is the more probable long-term outcome."
}
